{"chunk_id": "804c03c0cfa7", "text": "After completing his search and confirming Sita\u2019s presence, Hanuman considers how best to further harm the titans of Lanka before returning to Rama. Deciding that the destruction of the city will complete his mission, he uses the flames on his tail to ignite the mansions of the demon nobles. Leaping from roof to roof with immense speed, he sets ablaze the palaces of many powerful rakshasas and finally Ravana\u2019s own resplendent residence. The fire spreads across Lanka like a cosmic catastrophe, fanned by the wind, melting jewels and metals and sending the inhabitants into panic. Demons wonder if the blazing monkey is actually a god in disguise\u2014Agni, Indra, or even Vishnu\u2019s power. As the city burns, the heavens rejoice, praising Hanuman\u2019s divine strength and heroic devastation.\nHanuman uses the fire on his tail to burn Lanka, leaping across palaces and spreading a catastrophic blaze that terrifies the demons and devastates the city.\nThemes: divine retribution, heroic destruction, cosmic imagery, fear of divine power, devotion to Rama", "vector": [0.006440410856157541, -0.020540405064821243, 0.00021037350234109908, -0.00866672582924366, -0.0033659760374575853, 0.019864559173583984, -0.03554152697324753, -0.00027311284793540835, -0.010396094992756844, -0.012324242852628231, -0.002708351705223322, 0.027881942689418793, 0.017638245597481728, 0.011303848586976528, 0.01280131097882986, 0.003647578414529562, 0.04325411841273308, -0.016710612922906876, 0.013125981204211712, -0.01518664788454771, -0.017969541251659393, -0.006741891149431467, -0.008792618289589882, 0.004472507629543543, -0.007341538555920124, -0.001640747650526464, 0.01856587640941143, -0.048051297664642334, 0.006102487910538912, -0.0022097500041127205, 0.004339988809078932, -0.005837450735270977, -0.005463085137307644, 0.0015819425461813807, -0.023932885378599167, 0.010256950743496418, -0.0019347736379131675, 0.004412874113768339, -0.0046613467857